+composer (2.10.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium
+
+  freshdeb: this package installs composer.phar, built from Composer's
+  source the way upstream builds it, as /usr/bin/composer. The
+  distributions' packages installed Composer's PHP sources in
+  /usr/share/php instead, with Debian's php-composer-* and php-symfony-*
+  libraries; those libraries are no longer needed (apt autoremove), and of
+  Composer's classes only its class loader
+  (/usr/share/php/Composer/Autoload/ClassLoader.php) is still there for
+  other software. Projects that use Composer as a library should require
+  composer/composer themselves.
+
+  "composer self-update" is disabled: updates come with this package.
+
+  Changes since the distributions' versions that may need action:
+   * Updates refuse package versions with known security advisories
+     (config audit.block-insecure, default true since 2.9), and installs
+     refuse packages reported as malware (2.10).
+   * If a package's dist (zip) download fails, Composer no longer falls
+     back to cloning its source (config source-fallback, 2.10).
+   * "composer audit" exits with 0 or 1 only (2.10); its JSON output has
+     reportedAt as an RFC 3339 string (2.5).
+  Upstream's changelog has every change:
+  https://github.com/composer/composer/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md
+
+ -- freshdeb <packages@freshdeb.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
+
